{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall cast for it four rings of gold.</b> According to its plain sense, they are small rings that were part of the ark itself." "<b>On its four pa'amot.</b> On the two sides of its width. And some interpret <b>pa'amotav</b> as its feet, as in ״מה יפו פעמיך בנעלים״ (how beautiful are your feet in sandals), ״רגלי עני פעמי דלים״ (the feet of the poor, the steps of the needy). It is not fitting for the ark to rest directly on the ground. And two other large rings, to serve as housings for the poles — and these two rings are set into the small rings. And when they would set the ark down, the large rings would descend with the poles and hang there, so that the Holy One, blessed be He, did not want the ark to be supported by contact when the poles were in the rings." "<b>On its one side and two rings on its second side.</b> That is, on its four pa'amot. And the length of the ark ran from north to south, between the poles, whose length ran from east to west."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:22.966025043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}